cartridge "BOUNCE AWAY/CZES KOSNIOWSKI/1983"

' BOUNCE AWAY - ColecoVision version of the Oric game by Chris (Czes)
' Kosniowski ("Games to Play on Your Oric-1", Shiva, 1983, game 24).
' Adapted by Amy & Claude, Amy Studio 2026. Built by build.py from this
' file, ../_common/amy/core.alexis, pages.txt, art.py and music/*.txt.
'
' THE GAME (as in the book): rows of coloured bricks fill the top of the
' screen, obstacles are scattered below them, and a small bat moves left
' and right at the bottom. The ball bounces off the sides, the bricks, the
' obstacles and the bat; every brick it hits disappears. Get the ball to
' the top of the screen (WELL DONE). A ball that falls past the bat costs a
' chance (EXPLODE); the bricks stay as they are.
'
' CONTROLS: joystick left/right moves the bat, a button serves (the ball
' also goes by itself after 2.5 seconds). Title: up/down choose,
' left/right the starting level (the book's skill 1-4), a button confirms.
'
' LIBERTIES (listed for Amy):
' - Pixel movement instead of character cells. The book's ball only went
'   at 45 degrees; here the angle depends on where the ball meets the bat
'   (centre: steep, edges: wider), between about 20 and 45 degrees from
'   the vertical. The ball bounces off a brick or orb on the side it hit.
' - The obstacles (the book's '@', never removed by the listing although
'   the text says they "slowly disappear") are orbs that crack and vanish
'   after 2 hits (3 from level 3 on).
' - Field: 26 columns between two walls (the book: 36). Bricks: 3 rows at
'   level 1 (the book's skill 1) up to 6 rows (skill 4), 16 orbs.
' - Chances: 10 at level 1 (the book: 13 - skill - 2 = 10 for skill 1),
'   one less per starting level; one more for each level cleared (10 max).
'   After WELL DONE the game goes on to the next level (the book stopped),
'   with more rows of bricks and a faster ball.
' - The book's score was only the chances left; here bricks and orbs give
'   points too (HUD, right).
' - v2 (Amy's review): from level 3 the ball is faster in bigger steps,
'   orbs take 3 hits (4 from level 5), steel bricks (unbreakable, 2 more
'   a level, 8 at most) appear, and from level 5 the bat is 16 px wide.
' - Colour, animation, music and sound effects are new. The book's PING
'   (walls) and the three PINGs of WELL DONE are kept as cues.

' tile set Ba: 126 tiles from code 128, one copy per screen third (art.py)
